ENGLISH (informational translation)
================================================================================

1. SUBJECT

These terms cover the software "MinePower" including source code, Docker
images, documentation, artwork and name marks (together, "the Software"). The
source is publicly viewable, but the Software is not Open Source as defined by
the Open Source Definition: no rights to modify or redistribute are granted.

2. PERMITTED

Without separate consent you may:

   a) download, view and study the Software;
   b) run it unmodified on your own hardware or infrastructure — private or
      for your own business operations;
   c) run it unmodified from the official Docker image;
   d) create and use your own configuration files, settings and data.
      Configuration is not modification within the meaning of section 3.

3. NOT PERMITTED

Without prior written consent of the copyright holder you may not:

   a) modify, translate, adapt, decompile or create derivative works;
   b) redistribute, publish, rent, lend, sell or sublicense the Software or
      parts of it;
   c) provide the Software to third parties as a service (hosting, SaaS,
      managed service);
   d) remove or alter copyright, license or attribution notices;
   e) use the name "MinePower" or the MinePower mark for your own offerings.

   Platform note: where the Software is made available through a platform whose
   terms mandate certain acts (such as creating a copy within that platform),
   those terms prevail to that extent. No further rights are granted thereby.

4. FEEDBACK

Feedback is expressly welcome — bug reports, measurements, diagnostic reports,
suggestions. By submitting feedback you grant the copyright holder a free,
perpetual and worldwide right to use it without compensation or attribution.
There is no obligation to act on it.

Please do not include credentials, tokens or personal data. The built-in
diagnostic report redacts fields declared as passwords automatically, but
cannot know every field — please review before sending.

5. WARRANTY AND LIABILITY

THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, INCLUDING
WITHOUT LIMITATION MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE, OR
ABSENCE OF DEFECTS.

The Software controls electrical loads. Use is at your own risk. Installation
and protection of electrical components belongs in the hands of qualified
personnel; applicable standards and grid operator requirements must be
observed. The copyright holder is not liable for property, financial or
consequential damages arising from its use — except in cases of intent, gross
negligence, or where liability is mandatory by law.

A substantial share of the device integrations has never been exercised against
real hardware; they were written from vendor documentation. Which ones is
stated in the README and in the user interface at each device. Register maps
regularly deviate in practice — verify the live values before productive use.

6. THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS

The Software uses third-party components under their own licenses. These terms
do not change that. See the NOTICE file for details.

7. TRADEMARKS AND THIRD-PARTY INTERFACES

Tesla, Sungrow, my-PV, Fronius, SMA, Huawei, Shelly, go-e, KEBA, Tibber,
aWATTar and all other names mentioned are trademarks of their respective
owners. They are used purely descriptively to indicate which devices and
services the Software interoperates with. There is no affiliation with,
partnership with, or endorsement by these companies.

Anyone using those providers' interfaces (such as the Tesla Fleet API) enters
into their own relationship with that provider and is bound by its terms.
Credentials and tokens are supplied by the operator; the Software contains
none.

8. FINAL PROVISIONS

German law applies, excluding the UN Convention on Contracts for the
International Sale of Goods. If any provision is invalid, the remainder stays
in force.

Enquiries regarding different use, commercial licensing or modification: via
the GitHub project.
